  <p>
    The Grievance Officer is a member of the avaTOK team and is resident in
    India, as required by the Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media
    Ethics Code) Rules, 2021. Complaints sent to
    <a href="mailto:grievance@avatok.ai">grievance@avatok.ai</a> reach the Grievance Officer
    directly and are handled under the timelines below.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What you can complain about</h2>
  <p>You can use this channel to complain about:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Content on avaTOK that you believe is unlawful, or that breaches our
      <a href="/community-guidelines">Community Guidelines</a> or
      <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>.</li>
    <li>Content that infringes your intellectual property — you can also use our
      <a href="/dmca">DMCA / Copyright</a> process.</li>
    <li>Content that exposes your private information, impersonates you, or is otherwise
      defamatory, obscene, or invasive of your privacy.</li>
    <li>Intimate or sexual imagery of you shared without your consent, including morphed or
      AI-generated imagery — see the expedited timeline in section 4.</li>
    <li>Content or conduct involving a child — see also our
      <a href="/child-safety">Child Safety Standards</a>.</li>
    <li>How we have handled your personal data — see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
    <li>A decision we took on your account, content, listing, or payout, if you have already tried
      support and are not satisfied.</li>
    <li>How our service is functioning, or non-compliance by us with these Rules.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How to file a complaint</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:grievance@avatok.ai">grievance@avatok.ai</a> with the subject line
    <em>Grievance</em>. Include as much of the following as you can — an incomplete complaint takes
    longer, because we have to come back to you for the missing pieces.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your <strong>full name</strong> and the <strong>email address and phone number</strong>
      linked to your avaTOK account, if you have one.</li>
    <li>A clear <strong>description of the complaint</strong> and what harm it is causing.</li>
    <li>The <strong>exact location</strong> of the content — a link, the account handle, the group
      or chat, and the approximate date and time.</li>
    <li><strong>Screenshots or other evidence</strong>, where you have them.</li>
    <li>The <strong>relief you are seeking</strong> — for example removal of a specific item, or
      restoration of your account.</li>
    <li>Where you are complaining about content that concerns you personally, a statement that the
      information you have given is <strong>true and accurate</strong>.</li>
    <li>If you are complaining on someone else's behalf, your <strong>authority</strong> to do
      so.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please send one complaint per issue. Sending the same complaint repeatedly does not speed it up
    and makes the record harder to follow.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Timelines</h2>
  <p>Under the IT Rules, 2021 we will:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Stage</th><th>Timeline</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Acknowledge your complaint</td>
        <td><strong>Within 24 hours</strong> of receiving it</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Dispose of (resolve) the complaint</td>
        <td><strong>Within 15 days</strong> of receiving it</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Act on a complaint about non-consensual intimate imagery — nudity, a sexual act, or
          impersonation in an electronic form, including morphed or artificially generated images
        </td>
        <td><strong>Within 24 hours</strong> of receiving the complaint</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Act on a valid order from a court or an authorised government agency</td>
        <td>Within the period the order or the law specifies</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The 24-hour category is deliberately fast because the harm is immediate. If your complaint
    falls into it, say so clearly in the subject line and the first paragraph so it is not missed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a complaint requires more information from you, the clock on resolution is affected by
    how quickly we get it. We will tell you what we need.
  </p>

  <h2>5. What happens after you file</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>You receive an acknowledgement with a reference number.</li>
    <li>We review the complaint against our policies and applicable law, and look at the content or
      account concerned where we can access it.</li>
    <li>We take action where the complaint is made out — which may mean removing or disabling
      access to content, restricting or terminating an account, correcting information, or
      explaining why no action is warranted.</li>
    <li>We write to you with the outcome and the reasons for it.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Some content on avaTOK is private to its participants and not accessible to us. Where that is
    the case, we act on the account-level information available to us and preserve and disclose
    what we lawfully hold when required by valid legal process.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Escalation</h2>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with the outcome, reply to the same email thread with your reference
    number and tell us why, and the Grievance Officer will review it again.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you remain dissatisfied, you may pursue whatever remedies are available to you under Indian
    law, including approaching the Grievance Appellate Committee constituted under the IT Rules,
    2021, or the appropriate court or authority. Nothing on this page limits your legal rights.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Users outside India</h2>
  <p>
    avaTOK is operated entirely from India by an unregistered Indian business, so this grievance
    mechanism applies to everyone regardless of where you are. If you are outside India, the fastest
    route is still <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>; privacy requests go to
    <a href="mailto:privacy@avatok.ai">privacy@avatok.ai</a>. Complaints about serious harm will be
    actioned wherever they come from.
  </p>

